{
  "id": "sound_transmission_through_duct_walls",
  "title": "Sound Transmission through Duct Walls",
  "description": "Calculate sound pressure level in a room based on sound transmission from ducts to surrounding rooms using the formula: Lp = LN - TL - 10 log(A F / 4 Ad)",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "content": "Sound Transmission Loss through Duct Walls (dB)",
      "headers": [
        "Duct Sheet Thickness (mm)",
        "125 Hz",
        "250 Hz",
        "500 Hz",
        "1000 Hz"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          1.25,
          17,
          22,
          25,
          29
        ],
        [
          1,
          15,
          20,
          23,
          27
        ],
        [
          0.75,
          14,
          19,
          22,
          26
        ],
        [
          0.65,
          12,
          17,
          20,
          24
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "Sound Pressure Level Calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "LN",
          "label": "Sound Power Level in Duct (LN)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 80,
          "unit": "dB"
        },
        {
          "id": "TL",
          "label": "Transmission Loss through Duct Wall (TL)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 25,
          "unit": "dB"
        },
        {
          "id": "A",
          "label": "Room Absorption (A)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "m² Sabine"
        },
        {
          "id": "F",
          "label": "Cross Section Area of Duct (F)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.5,
          "unit": "m²"
        },
        {
          "id": "Ad",
          "label": "Surface Area of Duct (Ad)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 5,
          "unit": "m²"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "Lp",
          "label": "Sound Pressure Level in Room (Lp)",
          "formula": "inputs.LN - inputs.TL - 10 * Math.log10((inputs.A * inputs.F) / (4 * inputs.Ad))",
          "unit": "dB",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Formula\n\n**Lp = LN - TL - 10 log(A F / 4 Ad)**\n\nWhere:\n- **Lp** = Sound pressure level in room (dB)\n- **LN** = Sound power level in the duct (dB)\n- **TL** = Transmission loss through duct wall (dB)\n- **A** = Room absorption (m² Sabine)\n- **F** = Cross section area of duct (m²)\n- **Ad** = Surface area of duct (m²)\n\n## Notes\n\nThe acoustic performance of round and oval ducts is superior to rectangular ducts since their curved surfaces allow less breakout noise. Low-frequency sound is better contained in round ducts."
    }
  ]
}